						<tr>
							<td height="50" colspan="3" valign="top" class="windowbg2" align="left">Eventually I think people just get sick of how LONG everything takes in EQ, too.  Many of the time sinks aren&#039;t as bad as they use to be and exp can be earned faster, and it still seems to take forever to do much and to gain levels/abilities.  I think... wheeee... you mean if I grind for 5 or 6 hours, I can get this AA ability that will make my character one quarter of one percent better?  oh boy!  Eventually I can win this item or get this aug that takes my hit points for 12,000 to 12,040?  Yippee!!!  /sarcasm<br /><br />So much time is wasted trying to put together a good group, waiting on slow people to arrive, organizing a raid, CRing, rebuffing, and medding up, the actual fights in some cases, etc.  I&#039;ve just been losing patience with it.  I&#039;m finally getting EQ attention deficit disorder. <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Smileys/Rodcet/razz.gif" alt="Razz" border="0" />  I have to have both of my accounts up if for no other reason than it allows me to keep an eye on things on one monitor while I alt-tab out on the other to browse the web during downtimes.  It helps to have some good CDs playing too.  Oh, and alcohol... drinking helps!&nbsp; &nbsp;<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Smileys/Rodcet/cool.gif" alt="Cool" border="0" />&nbsp; Yeah, I still find that too many distractions are needed to keep things happening fast enough for me in EQ.  That can&#039;t be a good sign.</td>
